OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,A'Mogging' is Collins' word of the
OL,4,Ayear... but do you know what it means?
OL,5,
OL,6,F"Mogging", a word used playfully to
OL,7,Fmean outshining, outperforming or
OL,8,Fupstaging someone or something, has
OL,9,Fbeen named as word of the year by the
OL,10,FCollins English Dictionary.
OL,12,FA fast-growing slang word among members
OL,13,Fof Generations Z and Alpha - both
OL,14,Fonline and in everyday conversation -
OL,15,Fmogging went mainstream in 2026 with a
OL,16,F210% increase in its usage.
OL,18,FCollins' managing director Alex
OL,19,FBeecroft said its lexicographers look
OL,20,Fat "how often words are used" and also
OL,21,F"analyse patterns of usage" that reveal
OL,22,Fthe latest linguistic trends.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG12/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,163,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11913
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1793703248
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,A'Mogging' is Collins' word of the
OL,4,Ayear... but do you know what it means?
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe selection of mogging as word of the
OL,7,Fyear, he said, "shows how each
OL,8,Fgeneration leaves its mark on
OL,9,Flanguage".
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/19
